---
import landmarks from "../data/landmarks.json";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Vetlas & our data policy"
  description="What Vetlas is, how we label every fact with a trust tier, and why there are no ads or paid placements. Free forever, built for India."
  canonical="/about/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head text-center mx-auto">
      <span class="card-icon hero-mark">
        <Icon name="paw" class="icon icon-xl" />
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-1">About Vetlas</h1>
      <p class="mx-auto">
        Vetlas is an independent, ten-city veterinary care discovery platform — not an ad
        platform. Our goal: when your pet is unwell, help you choose the right care quickly, with
        clearly attributed and trustworthy data.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doc mt-25 pb-1">
      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="badge" class="icon icon-lg" /> Our data policy</h2>
        <p>
          Listing details and expandable evidence sections distinguish these data categories:
        </p>
        <p class="stack mt-09">
          <span><strong>Verified</strong> — credentials checked by hand by the Vetlas team, with the date checked shown.</span>
          <span><strong>Provider-confirmed</strong> — details claimed and confirmed directly by the provider.</span>
          <span><strong>Public source</strong> — from public web pages, maps or directories, with fetch date and link.</span>
          <span><strong>User-submitted</strong> — moderated reports from pet owners.</span>
          <span><strong>Estimated</strong> — system-calculated ranges, shown only above minimum sample sizes.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          The directory uses public listings and preserves source provenance. Vetlas does not
          independently verify medical quality, and it never invents provider information, reviews,
          ratings or pricing. Missing prices invite you to ask the clinic. Historical and conflicting prices carry a short label and are excluded from numeric fee comparisons.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="shield" class="icon icon-lg" /> No ads, no paid placement</h2>
        <p>
          Providers cannot pay for higher rankings or to hide reviews. Results follow data —
          trust level, review themes and fees — never money. Vetlas is free to use, forever.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="sparkle" class="icon icon-lg" /> Themes over stars</h2>
        <p>
          No first-party reviews have been published yet. External community discussions are linked with attribution and branch uncertainty. Verified review themes will be introduced after moderated evidence is available.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="clock" class="icon icon-lg" /> Built for the hard days</h2>
        <p>
          Most people find a vet for the first time during an emergency. Vetlas is optimised for
          that moment: fast search, 24×7 filters, fee transparency and a clear path to the right
          speciality. No popups, no lead-capture walls, no sponsored cards.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block" id="animal-photo-credits">
        <h2>Photography</h2>
        <p>Facility images link to their original listing. Doctor portraits are attributed on each doctor profile. The animal portraits on the home page are cropped from the following photographs. Each crop uses its source licence.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dog_00154.JPG">Dog in Howrah</a> · Biswarup Ganguly · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Domestic_short_hair.jpg">Domestic shorthair</a> · Andrewwforsale · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gir_bull_2.jpg">Gir bull</a> · Chovatiyahiren · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holland_Lop_Bunny_Standing_On_Her_Back_Feet.jpg">Holland Lop rabbit</a> · SirDukeOfAwe · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cockatiel_3.jpg">Cockatiel</a> · Ganatron, <a href="https://paulweberphoto.com/">Paul Weber Photography</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spotted_deer_(Axis_axis)_male.jpg">Chital in Kanha National Park</a> · Charles J. Sharp, Sharp Photography · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Suggest a provider</h2>
        <p>
          Community submissions open soon. If you'd like to flag a great clinic or doctor — or
          correct something you see — the repository is public and issues are welcome.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary mt-1" href="/search/">Start exploring</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
<section id="landmark-credits" class="container"><h2>City landmark photography</h2><p>Images are resized and cropped for the city directory.</p><ul>{Object.entries(landmarks).map(([city,p]) => <li><a href={p.source}>{p.name}</a> · {city} · {p.author} · <a href={p.license==="FAL" ? "https://artlibre.org/licence/lal/en/" : "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/"+(p.license.includes("SA")?"by-sa":"by")+"/"+p.license.split(" ").at(-1)+"/"}>{p.license}</a></li>)}</ul></section></BaseLayout>
